course: dictionary
lesson: 8491
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Sandwich is a good example. Most often it means food: two slices of bread with something in between, such as cheese or ham. «Pack a cheese sandwich for the picnic.»
explain: Sandwich can also be a verb, a word for an action. To be sandwiched is to be squeezed between two things or people. «The pencil is a rod of graphite and clay sandwiched between two slats of cedar wood.» Nothing is eaten here. The clue is between two slats, which tells you the meaning.
explain: How do you know which meaning is right? Read the words around it. Food words, like cheese, bread or picnic, point to the food meaning. Words about squeezing, or being stuck between things, point to the other meaning. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: Some words are both a noun (a thing) and a verb (an action).
fact: «Sandwich» as a noun means two slices of bread with food such as cheese, ham or jam between them.
fact: «Sandwiched» as a verb means squeezed between two things or people.
fact: «Sandwich» is used in everyday life too: a packed lunch, a picnic, a sandwich shop.
fact: Sandwiches are named after the Earl of Sandwich, an English lord from long ago.
exercise: «Pack a cheese sandwich for the picnic.» What is a sandwich here? | A squeeze between two people | *Two slices of bread with food between them | A roll with no filling | A ship with sails
exercise: «The pencil is a rod of graphite sandwiched between two slats of cedar wood.» What does sandwiched mean here? | Bought from a shop | Eaten with bread | *Squeezed between two things | Painted bright red
exercise: Which word in «The bus was sandwiched between two lorries» tells you the bus was stuck in the middle? | was | lorries | *sandwiched | bus
test: «My sister was sandwiched between two tall men in the queue.» What does sandwiched mean? | A picnic on the grass | Two slices of bread with jam | *Squeezed between two people | A packed lunch for the bus
test: «The sandwich shop is open until five.» What does sandwich mean here? | A kind of ship | *Food made with bread and a filling | Painted and glued together | To be squeezed between two things
exam: Gran says the castle looked like «a sandwich made by a tornado». What does the picture suggest? | Kept safe and dry on a shelf | *Squashed and piled up in a messy heap | A tasty lunch with cheese | Neat rows of bread in a box
